{
  "id": "verdiales_malaga",
  "name": "Verdiales (Málaga hill-country pandas)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Verdiales is the fandango music of the Montes de Málaga and the neighbouring hill country, played by pandas: bands of violin, guitars, laúd, a large pandero frame drum, small cymbals and castanets, led by an alcalde with a staff, while a singer delivers fandango verses and couples dance. Its three styles are named after Montes, Almogía and Comares; the pandas meet every 28 December at the Fiesta Mayor de Verdiales, the tradition is inscribed as a Bien de Interés Cultural, and verdiales are commonly described as a root of the malagueña. The bandurria card stands in for the laúd.",
  "recipe": "classic modern verdiales, functional Song, iberian branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. fiddle, classical nylon-string guitar, bandurria, pandero source unspecified, credited cymbals, castanets. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
